WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:05.530
This dragon has fought every kind of 
Word on every kind of battlefield,

00:05.530 --> 00:06.970
and defeated them all.

00:08.220 --> 00:09.360
This...

00:10.260 --> 00:12.520
This is... a dragon.

00:51.320 --> 00:56.870
The Faraway Paladin

00:53.160 --> 00:56.870
<b><u>The Lord of the Rust Mountains</u></b>

01:46.160 --> 01:53.000
The Evil Dragon and the Goddess

01:46.350 --> 01:49.770
Well, now, Faraway Paladin...

01:50.420 --> 01:53.330
You have fought bravely. I commend you.

01:55.710 --> 01:58.460
Out of respect for the 
fight you have put up,

01:58.460 --> 02:00.340
I offer you this proposal.

02:03.800 --> 02:08.480
Have you any interest in serving me?

02:10.200 --> 02:12.440
I see that you are wise to my intentions.

02:13.080 --> 02:15.870
I am prepared to give you justification.

02:18.090 --> 02:20.480
Should you refuse to accept my proposal,

02:20.860 --> 02:26.630
I will burn your companions' 
very bones and souls to ashes.

02:27.240 --> 02:30.720
Thus threatened, you had no choice 
but to capitulate to the dragon

02:30.720 --> 02:33.490
in order to save your companions' lives.

02:33.870 --> 02:38.510
Well? It serves as an appropriate 
excuse, does it not?

02:41.440 --> 02:45.720
I have seen many humans with 
that very look in their eyes.

02:46.340 --> 02:49.870
Even if I threaten to burn 
you to ashes yourself,

02:49.870 --> 02:52.710
you will not bend or falter.

02:53.360 --> 02:57.420
You are still trying to ensure that 
your companions do not catch on

02:57.420 --> 03:01.990
as you continue to search for a 
way out of this predicament.

03:01.990 --> 03:07.620
But no matter how hard you try, 
your effort is in vain.

03:07.620 --> 03:09.220
Am I wrong?

03:10.700 --> 03:14.640
No... There is one way

03:14.640 --> 03:16.890
for you to avoid giving in to me.

03:20.160 --> 03:22.370
You need only kill yourself.

03:25.160 --> 03:28.880
You are loved by the goddess 
of flux, are you not?

03:28.880 --> 03:32.340
Simply cut off your own head.

03:32.910 --> 03:35.740
After all, the next world awaits you, yes?

03:35.740 --> 03:38.390
And the next one after that?

03:38.390 --> 03:45.350
And after that, and after that—
you have infinite chances, do you not?

03:45.350 --> 03:47.580
If you wish to prevent tragedy,

03:47.580 --> 03:52.120
simply end your life, as you would throw 
a game board if you could not win.

03:52.120 --> 03:58.800
Tell yourself, "Not here. Next time. 
This is not the time for me to fight."

03:58.800 --> 04:00.790
I won't choose that.

04:01.140 --> 04:02.840
Very well, then.

04:03.370 --> 04:07.330
One who sees his own life as 
no more valuable than that

04:07.330 --> 04:09.270
is not worth having in my service.

04:11.610 --> 04:13.680
Choose, then.

04:14.150 --> 04:16.240
Will you side with me,

04:16.730 --> 04:19.570
or will you fight me and die?

04:19.950 --> 04:23.980
I can well imagine what would 
happen if I sided with you.

04:23.980 --> 04:25.790
I cannot bow to you.

04:26.240 --> 04:28.400
Your companions will die.

04:28.900 --> 04:32.190
We came here prepared for that possibility.

04:32.190 --> 04:34.070
If any of us are lost,

04:34.070 --> 04:38.450
so long as just one of us survives to put 
a blade to your throat, that's enough.

04:39.010 --> 04:43.120
But surely you see that you 
have no chance of winning.

04:44.660 --> 04:45.740
I do.

04:46.180 --> 04:52.830
If I hit you thousands—millions—
of times with this blade, I will win.

04:53.660 --> 04:54.970
Am I wrong?

04:57.010 --> 05:02.090
Perhaps after many thousands of miracles.

05:02.090 --> 05:06.310
It doesn't matter how many thousands, 
millions, or billions it takes.

05:06.310 --> 05:10.290
If I have a chance at winning, 
at keeping my promise,

05:10.290 --> 05:12.070
I will bet on it.

05:12.300 --> 05:16.290
You're about to see how stubborn I can be.

05:18.810 --> 05:20.820
Evil dragon Valacirca!

05:21.180 --> 05:23.960
Faraway Paladin.

05:23.960 --> 05:26.980
I will slay you!

05:30.390 --> 05:32.980
I will strike you down before you can!

05:33.470 --> 05:34.730
<b>Strong Life</b>

05:33.470 --> 05:34.730
Fortis Vita!

05:37.020 --> 05:38.260
Acceleratio!

05:37.020 --> 05:38.270
<b>Accelerate</b>

05:41.520 --> 05:43.150
<b>Falling Spiderweb</b>

05:41.520 --> 05:43.150
Cadere Araneum!

05:54.490 --> 05:56.850
<i>I need to try to keep them out of this!</i>

05:59.830 --> 06:00.960
<b>Words Fly</b>

05:59.830 --> 06:00.960
Verba Volanto!

06:01.630 --> 06:02.590
<b>Thunder</b>

06:01.630 --> 06:02.590
Tonitrus!

06:16.430 --> 06:17.520
<b>Devastate</b>

06:16.430 --> 06:17.520
Vastare!

06:38.000 --> 06:39.250
<b>Accelerate</b>

06:38.000 --> 06:39.250
Acceleratio!

06:57.300 --> 06:58.650
<i>Pale Moon...</i>

07:06.320 --> 07:09.230
<i>Valacirca is wounded all over, too.</i>

07:09.230 --> 07:13.870
<i>If I can just get Overeater into him 
somewhere and extract his life force...</i>

07:14.830 --> 07:17.130
Truly a shame.

07:27.120 --> 07:31.120
I am familiar with that demonblade.

07:31.560 --> 07:35.470
It is quite a threat, indeed.

07:36.750 --> 07:41.390
It is said to have been 
forged by a demon king

07:41.390 --> 07:47.250
in order to confront and kill 
the sword-obsessed High King.

07:48.390 --> 07:51.690
But if one knows how it works,

07:51.690 --> 07:53.410
it can be defeated.

07:53.410 --> 07:54.900
Much like this.

08:01.190 --> 08:05.190
<i>I guess he has no intention of 
fighting at close range anymore.</i>

08:06.370 --> 08:08.860
While it has been entertaining,

08:08.860 --> 08:16.240
I never dreamed a mere human could 
make a fight so difficult,

08:16.950 --> 08:22.070
Faraway Paladin, William G. Maryblood.

08:22.070 --> 08:24.680
<i>My mana's already...</i>

08:24.990 --> 08:29.680
I commend you for giving me so many wounds.

08:30.040 --> 08:34.800
Were we merely testing each other's skills,

08:34.800 --> 08:38.110
I might have placed a wreath 
of victory on your head

08:38.110 --> 08:41.150
for putting up such a 
fight against a dragon.

08:41.450 --> 08:46.060
Your strength rivals that of the 
heroes of the age of gods.

08:46.540 --> 08:50.080
You are a true man of power—

08:50.080 --> 08:52.320
a hero of the present age!

08:53.020 --> 08:54.340
However...

08:55.480 --> 08:59.080
This is a battle to the death!

09:02.550 --> 09:05.050
I will not make you suffer.

09:05.050 --> 09:07.300
At the very least, you can...

09:07.850 --> 09:09.820
die quickly!

09:11.750 --> 09:15.010
<i>I swore an oath to the goddess!</i>

09:24.230 --> 09:28.980
A Herald? Too weak to send an Echo, then?

09:28.980 --> 09:32.890
A wasted effort, goddess of light!

09:45.820 --> 09:47.940
<i>Goddess...</i>

09:49.580 --> 09:53.710
You value your hero's life that much?

09:54.100 --> 10:01.980
But the intervention of a mere Herald 
from a single god changes nothing!

10:14.060 --> 10:15.580
Paladin...

10:16.310 --> 10:21.050
You have proven yourself 
worthy to die by my breath.

10:21.710 --> 10:25.580
I will hold your image within my memory,

10:25.580 --> 10:30.730
but I will burn you to ash, 
body and soul, down to the last bone!

10:30.730 --> 10:33.150
No, no. I can't have that.

10:33.740 --> 10:35.110
Who goes there?!

10:45.290 --> 10:49.980
This hero is my prey. My enemy.

10:50.530 --> 10:54.220
I am certain of that 
after seeing him fight.

10:54.660 --> 10:58.420
And I won't have him defeated by 
another right in front of me.

10:58.810 --> 11:02.760
The god of the undead, Stagnate?!

11:07.510 --> 11:12.110
Well, now, evil dragon Valacirca...

11:12.570 --> 11:20.120
I believe you said the intervention of a 
mere Herald from a single god changes nothing.

11:21.750 --> 11:23.430
You are right.

11:23.430 --> 11:26.190
That is the prophecy I gave him, as well.

11:26.190 --> 11:28.580
Heroes are insufficient,

11:28.580 --> 11:32.250
and heroes with the goddess of light 
on their side are still insufficient.

11:32.720 --> 11:37.010
They stand no chance of slaying the 
evil dragon, Calamity's Sickle.

11:37.010 --> 11:38.410
But come to think of it,

11:38.410 --> 11:42.970
I didn't consider what the intervention 
of <i>two</i> gods could do.

11:42.970 --> 11:44.480
I wonder what would change.

11:45.080 --> 11:48.600
Would these heroes have 
a chance of winning?

11:48.600 --> 11:54.300
I believe they would have at 
least some chance, Valacirca.

11:54.300 --> 11:58.730
You are as loquacious as ever, 
god of the undead.

11:58.980 --> 12:02.910
You and I are two of a kind. 
A detestable kind.

12:02.910 --> 12:05.530
I feel we have similar tastes.

12:05.530 --> 12:08.490
My taste is not as bad as yours.

12:08.990 --> 12:14.210
A life—a soul—only has value if 
it burns out with a final twinkle.

12:14.630 --> 12:19.410
What is the point of living 
forever, you worldly fool?

12:19.410 --> 12:21.830
That itself is poor taste.

12:21.830 --> 12:24.410
Beautiful things should last forever.

12:24.410 --> 12:27.430
That is natural. You only seek to destroy.

12:29.060 --> 12:33.100
What a lady killer you are, paladin.

12:33.100 --> 12:36.210
Even in the age of gods, 
I never saw the like.

12:36.210 --> 12:40.730
Imagine! <i>Two</i> goddesses rushing to 
your side when you are in peril!

12:40.730 --> 12:41.790
Goddess?

12:43.890 --> 12:48.240
Does it matter whether I 
am a god or a goddess?

12:48.240 --> 12:53.410
To a god, gender is only decorative. Right?

12:55.340 --> 12:58.250
Don't be so angry, Gracefeel.

12:58.250 --> 13:01.420
Where's the harm in enjoying 
a little perk like this?

13:02.570 --> 13:06.040
"Why now?" you ask?

13:06.040 --> 13:09.230
After seeing such a furious battle,

13:09.230 --> 13:12.160
I would regret <i>not</i> intervening much more.

13:12.650 --> 13:19.210
You would interfere in the great Valacirca's 
fight for a reason like that?

13:19.210 --> 13:22.280
You hero-obsessed hedonist!

13:22.280 --> 13:23.780
Precisely.

13:23.780 --> 13:29.870
This hero, this strange paladin, 
is worth going mad for.

13:30.670 --> 13:34.220
Now, this battle is not yet over.

13:34.220 --> 13:36.640
Do you have the will to fight once more,

13:37.090 --> 13:39.630
William G. Maryblood?

13:39.920 --> 13:42.850
My foolish yet clever enemy,

13:42.850 --> 13:44.880
paladin of the light...

13:44.880 --> 13:47.910
Uphold your vow and hold your 
conviction in your heart.

13:47.910 --> 13:52.780
You stated that you would fight until 
the moment you fell over dead.

13:52.780 --> 13:55.670
Surely that was not a lie, was it?

13:57.790 --> 14:01.270
I can't get out of doing this, can I?

14:01.940 --> 14:03.230
Valacirca!

14:03.670 --> 14:04.980
What?

14:05.440 --> 14:08.720
Remember when I said you were about 
to see how stubborn I can be?

14:12.970 --> 14:16.450
Indeed, you are dreadfully stubborn!

14:16.450 --> 14:20.750
Was it this persistence that set 
the gods in action at last?

14:20.750 --> 14:23.050
You truly are a hero!

14:23.790 --> 14:25.290
Very well.

14:25.290 --> 14:28.820
The gods have given you their 
utmost blessings and protection,

14:28.820 --> 14:32.820
allowing a man and a dragon 
to stand as equals.

14:32.820 --> 14:36.740
And burning the hero lauded by the gods

14:36.740 --> 14:39.110
is what makes me a dragon!

14:39.480 --> 14:44.090
Now, merciful goddesses 
who oversee the soul!

14:44.090 --> 14:47.020
Lovely maidens who have lost 
the protection of war!

14:47.020 --> 14:50.480
What protections will you give this hero?

14:50.480 --> 14:52.670
How will you kill me?

14:52.670 --> 14:54.110
I won't give him any.

14:56.070 --> 14:59.260
This man is my enemy.

14:59.260 --> 15:02.370
He declared that he always would be.

15:02.370 --> 15:05.870
I have no reason to grant 
him any protection.

15:05.870 --> 15:07.380
Oh?

15:07.380 --> 15:11.030
But surely you haven't 
forgotten, Valacirca,

15:11.380 --> 15:13.740
where you are right now?

15:14.760 --> 15:17.810
Yes! This is the Iron Country!

15:17.810 --> 15:21.550
The mountains where the regretful souls 
of the warriors of flame reside!

15:22.860 --> 15:25.290
Now is the time to return!

15:25.290 --> 15:29.170
Your compatriots, 
your descendants, have come back!

15:29.170 --> 15:32.600
They have brought one who 
is undeniably a hero

15:32.600 --> 15:35.620
to defeat the demons, challenge the dragon,

15:35.620 --> 15:38.460
and take back the mountains they call home!

15:39.390 --> 15:43.540
A warrior should not wander about, asleep, 
and merely observe such an event!

15:43.540 --> 15:47.120
Now, take up the sword of vengeance!

15:47.340 --> 15:50.880
Set the flames of courage ablaze once more,

15:51.250 --> 15:53.640
dwarven warriors!

16:17.070 --> 16:19.770
You haven't become undead, have you?

16:20.890 --> 16:23.560
Relax. We're alive.

16:23.560 --> 16:25.250
Yes, as you can see.

16:25.250 --> 16:27.260
Cut it pretty close, though.

16:27.260 --> 16:30.760
That solo battle of yours 
distracted the dragon.

16:30.760 --> 16:34.100
And then, with the protection 
of our ancestral god...

16:34.100 --> 16:37.250
It took a while, since I'm not used 
to it, but I healed us all.

16:37.250 --> 16:38.480
I see.

16:39.000 --> 16:42.270
Al, when you were fighting that demon,

16:42.590 --> 16:45.180
you earned the divine protection 
of Blaze, god of fire.

16:45.660 --> 16:46.510
Yes.

16:47.580 --> 16:50.050
Sir William, what is this?

16:50.740 --> 16:54.210
They're our allies. 
Reinforcements we can rely on.

17:14.960 --> 17:17.370
Grandfather...

17:38.090 --> 17:38.970
Huh?

17:40.290 --> 17:43.050
Shouldn't you give that to Al?

18:01.830 --> 18:02.980
Calldawn.

18:03.720 --> 18:08.390
An enchanted sword handed down among 
the dwarfs since the age of gods,

18:08.390 --> 18:10.560
and the blade that took 
one of Valacirca's eyes.

18:11.570 --> 18:13.900
Hero of the light...

18:14.570 --> 18:18.380
Take care of my grandson... 
and these mountains.

18:18.380 --> 18:19.660
Please.

18:24.080 --> 18:25.320
Grandfather!

18:25.890 --> 18:29.210
Valacirca's flames burn 
everything up, even souls.

18:29.210 --> 18:30.570
No...

18:31.270 --> 18:32.280
Not yet.

18:33.110 --> 18:34.590
It's not over yet.

18:40.980 --> 18:42.550
Goddess...

18:42.840 --> 18:46.820
Hear me, you who cannot 
preserve your souls.

18:47.420 --> 18:49.470
You who have been burned 
by the dragon's breath

18:49.470 --> 18:51.850
and cannot return to the cycle of rebirth.

18:52.300 --> 18:55.350
You who were born into this 
world, who lived well,

18:55.350 --> 18:56.930
and lived to the fullest.

18:57.310 --> 19:00.080
I bestow upon you this final blessing.

19:00.080 --> 19:03.000
If, even in death, 
even after your souls have perished,

19:03.000 --> 19:06.320
you still wish to pursue 
what is good and right...

19:06.560 --> 19:08.070
I shall guide you!

19:08.070 --> 19:12.160
Gather under the heroes who 
live in the present day!

19:44.120 --> 19:45.740
Grandfather...

19:47.030 --> 19:50.000
I will not apologize.

19:51.040 --> 19:52.670
My grandson...

19:53.120 --> 19:55.460
Look after our country, 
and all of our people.

19:57.740 --> 19:59.110
Please.

20:04.430 --> 20:05.230
I will.

20:09.330 --> 20:10.810
You can count on me.

20:24.890 --> 20:26.380
Sheesh...

20:26.810 --> 20:30.770
I guess she could never 
let me have all the fun.

20:38.640 --> 20:40.920
It seems you are ready,

20:41.220 --> 20:43.340
Faraway Paladin.

20:43.970 --> 20:47.160
You weren't just being nice, were you?

20:48.710 --> 20:52.920
Certainly not. I merely like 
to let my wine age a bit.

20:54.020 --> 20:57.430
Once you have made your preparations 
and gathered all you need,

20:57.780 --> 21:03.440
you, the heroes, come for me filled 
with hope, and I crush you.

21:03.440 --> 21:07.960
The moment your faces distort in despair...

21:07.960 --> 21:14.190
For me, that is the greatest joy!

21:15.170 --> 21:20.710
Now, challenge me once 
more, Faraway Paladin!

21:20.710 --> 21:25.970
Will I kill all of you and add a 
new entry to a history of terror,

21:25.970 --> 21:29.360
or will you slay me and be celebrated

21:29.360 --> 21:32.440
for your tremendous feat 
until the end of time?

21:33.440 --> 21:36.980
Now is the time to finish this battle!

21:40.310 --> 21:41.580
I'm going.

21:41.580 --> 21:44.460
Yes. I order you once more:

21:45.720 --> 21:46.710
Go.

21:46.940 --> 21:49.730
Slay the dragon and keep your promise,

21:49.730 --> 21:51.220
my knight.

21:52.410 --> 21:55.650
On my sword, on the light,

21:55.650 --> 21:58.980
on the souls of the warriors 
that dwell within my chest...

21:59.430 --> 22:02.430
I will slay the evil dragon!

23:35.640 --> 23:39.930
Calldawn
